    <string name="help_q1">How do I add a SIP account?</string>
    <string name="help_a1">Settings → Account → Manage SIP accounts → Add. Enter the server (domain), username and password from your SIP provider. When the top bar of the home page shows Online, you can call.</string>
    <string name="help_q2">It shows Offline or Failed</string>
    <string name="help_a2">Check the server, username and password. Try another transport (UDP, TCP or TLS) in the account settings and check your internet. Settings → App logs shows the reason given by the server.</string>
    <string name="help_q3">Calls do not ring when the app is closed</string>
    <string name="help_a3">Allow all permissions and background running in Settings → Permissions. On Xiaomi, Oppo, Samsung and similar phones also set the app to Autostart and No restrictions in the phone settings. Open the app once after the phone restarts.</string>
    <string name="help_q4">No sound, or only one side can hear</string>
    <string name="help_a4">Allow the microphone permission. Try the speaker or earpiece button during the call. If the problem continues, try TCP or TLS transport, or ask your SIP provider about NAT and firewall settings.</string>
    <string name="help_q5">Where are call recordings?</string>
    <string name="help_a5">Settings → Call recording → Recordings. You can play, share or delete them. Record calls only with the other person\'s consent.</string>
    <string name="help_q6">How do forwarding, Do Not Disturb and blocking work?</string>
    <string name="help_a6">They are handled by this app, so they only work while the app is running and online. Blocked numbers are checked first, then forwarding, then Do Not Disturb.</string>
    <string name="help_q7">How do I move to a new phone?</string>
    <string name="help_a7">Settings → Backup &amp; restore → Export (use a passphrase), copy the file to the new phone and use Import.</string>
